#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# find_sequence_function

#% text
# `find_sequence_function(xs, n)` gives a closed form `f(n)` with `f(1) = xs[1]`, `f(2) = xs[2]`, ...

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The search covers polynomials, polynomials divided by `n` or `n + 1`, and such expressions times `n!`, `fibonacci(n)`, `(-1)^n` or `c^n` for `c` = 2, 3, 4, 5; then sequences whose differences are geometric, `a + b r^n` with `r` a number or a symbol.

#% item
# A list of pairs `[[x1, y1], [x2, y2], ...]` with equally spaced `x` gives the function of the `y` written in `x`.

#% item
# When every second term is 0, the other terms are searched and the result carries the factor `(1 - (-1)^n)/2` or `(1 + (-1)^n)/2`.

#% item
# Rational terms that satisfy a linear recurrence with polynomial coefficients (order up to 4, degree up to 4, at least two equations beyond the unknowns) give the solution of that recurrence by `r_solve_value`, or its `difference_root` when there is no closed form; either gives every listed term.

#% item
# At least two terms beyond those fixing the form must agree, so the list needs at least three terms.

#% item
# When nothing fits the result is `failure(no_sequence_function, xs)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
find_sequence_function([1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13], n)
#% output
#= fibonacci(n)

#% cell
find_sequence_function([2, 5, 10, 17, 26, 37, 50], n)
#% output
#= 1 + n^2

#% cell
find_sequence_function([2, 5/2, 10/3, 17/4, 26/5, 37/6, 50/7], n)
#% output
#= (1 + n^2)/n

#% cell
find_sequence_function([1, 2, 6, 24, 120, 720, 5040], n)
#% output
#= factorial(n)

#% cell
find_sequence_function([-1, 1, -1, 1, -1, 1], n)
#% output
#= (-1)^n

#% cell
find_sequence_function([2, 6, 12, 20, 30, 42], k)
#% output
#= k + k^2

#% cell
find_sequence_function([1 + a, 1 + a^2, 1 + a^3, 1 + a^4, 1 + a^5], n)
#% output
#= 1 + a^n

#% cell
find_sequence_function([2/3, 4/9, 8/27, 16/81, 32/243], n)
#% output
#= (2/3)^n

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
find_sequence_function(table([2 k, 2^k], [k, 10]), n)
#% output
#= 2^((1/2)*n)

#% cell
find_sequence_function([1, 0, 1, 0, 1/2, 0, 1/6, 0, 1/24, 0, 1/120], n)
#% output
#= (1 - (-1)^n)/(2*factorial(-1 + (1/2)*(1 + n)))

#% cell
find_sequence_function([1, 3, 10, 35, 126, 462, 1716, 6435, 24310], n)
#% output
#= pochhammer(3/2, -1 + n)*4^(-1 + n)/pochhammer(2, -1 + n)

#% cell
find_sequence_function([0, 1, 3, 8, 19, 43, 94, 201, 423, 880], n)
#% output
#= -2*(1/2)^n*(1 + 5^(1/2))^n/(-5 + 3*5^(1/2)) + 2*(1/2)^n*(1 - 5^(1/2))^n/(5 + 3*5^(1/2)) + 2^n

#% cell
find_sequence_function(table(factorial(k) + 1/k, [k, 14]), n)
#% output
#= difference_root((FormalY, FormalN) => [1 + FormalN + FormalN^2 + (-FormalN - 2*FormalN^2 - FormalN^3)*FormalY(FormalN) + (FormalN + FormalN^2)*FormalY(1 + FormalN) == 0, FormalY(1) == 2])(n)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `recurrence_table`, `interpolation`, `fit`, `find_linear_recurrence`, `difference_root`, `r_solve_value`
